IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc16-production-orders.l4 -- sections 487.014 to 487.03 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XV): the production orders, conditions, orders prohibiting disclosure, particulars,
-- review of orders, destruction of preserved data, the offences, and the assistance order.
-- Part agent ccc16. Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Imports the keel's core only (the definitions of section 487.011 are in ccc16-preservation.l4).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Conventions: as in ccc16-open-court.l4 and ccc16-preservation.l4. A bar for the person asking ("may not be made subject to an order") answers JUST TRUE where they are under investigation; "without lawful excuse" is a limit on
-- an offence: with a lawful excuse the section answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-10-29, marginal reading (b)). "As soon as feasible" and "as soon as practicable" state no number, so none is invented.
-- Seams: `s 2 terrorism offence` and `s 2 criminal organization offence` (MAYBE BOOLEAN), `s 489.1` and `s 490` (ccc17) are named only as provisions.

§ `Section 487.014 -- General production order`

-- 487.014(1) Subject to sections 487.015 to 487.018, on ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a person to produce a document that is a copy of a document that is in their possession or control when
-- they receive the order, or to prepare and produce a document containing data that is in their possession or control at that time.
-- src:9119 | General production order
-- src:9120 | 487.014 (1) Subject to sections 487.015 to 487.018, on ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a person to produce a document that is a copy of a document that is in their possession or control when they receive the order, or to prepare and produce a document containing data that is in their possession or control at that time.
@ref s 487.014(1) (src:9119-9120)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or data is in the person's possession or control when they receive the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is one for which section 487.015, 487.016, 487.017 or 487.018 provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.014(1) the justice or judge may order the person to produce a document or to prepare and produce a document` MEANS
    IF `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer` AND `the document or data is in the person's possession or control when they receive the order` AND (NOT `the order is one for which section 487.015, 487.016, 487.017 or 487.018 provides`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to sections 487.015 to 487.018, on ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a person to produce a document"

-- src:9121 | Conditions for making order
-- src:9122 | (2) Before making the order, the justice or judge must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004 that there are reasonable grounds to believe that
-- src:9123 | (a) an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament; and
-- src:9124 | (b) the document or data is in the person’s possession or control and will afford evidence respecting the commission of the offence.
@ref s 487.014(2) (src:9121-9124)
GIVEN `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the document or data is in the person's possession or control and will afford evidence respecting the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.014(2) the justice or judge has the satisfaction required before making the order` MEANS
    IF `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004`
       AND `there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament`
       AND `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the document or data is in the person's possession or control and will afford evidence respecting the commission of the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004"

-- src:9125 | Form
-- src:9126 | (3) The order is to be in Form 5.005.
@ref s 487.014(3) (src:9125-9126)
GIVEN `the order is in Form 5.005` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.014(3) the order is in Form 5.005` MEANS
    IF `the order is in Form 5.005`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The order is to be in Form 5.005"

-- src:9127 | Limitation
-- src:9128 | (4) A person who is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2) may not be made subject to an order.
@ref s 487.014(4) (src:9127-9128)
GIVEN `the person is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.014(4) the order is barred against the person under investigation for the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2) may not be made subject to an order"


§ `Section 487.0141 -- Production order -- specified dates`

-- src:9129 | Production order — specified dates
-- src:9130 | 487.0141 (1) On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a person to produce a document that is a copy of a document that is in their possession or control on any of the dates specified in the order or prepare and produce a document containing data that is in their possession or control on any of the dates specified in the order.
@ref s 487.0141(1) (src:9129-9130)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or data is in the person's possession or control on any of the dates specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0141(1) the justice or judge may order the person to produce a document on any of the dates specified in the order` MEANS
    IF `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer` AND `the document or data is in the person's possession or control on any of the dates specified in the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a person to produce a document that is a copy of a document that is in their possession or control on any of the dates specified in the order"

-- src:9131 | Conditions for making order
-- src:9132 | (2) Before making the order, the justice or judge must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004 that there are reasonable grounds to believe that
-- src:9133 | (a) an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament; and
-- src:9134 | (b) the document or data, if it is in the person’s possession or control on any of the dates to be specified in the order, will afford evidence respecting the commission of the offence.
@ref s 487.0141(2) (src:9131-9134)
GIVEN `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the document or data, if it is in the person's possession or control on any of the dates to be specified in the order, will afford evidence respecting the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0141(2) the justice or judge has the satisfaction required before making the order` MEANS
    IF `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004`
       AND `there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament`
       AND `there are reasonable grounds to believe that the document or data, if it is in the person's possession or control on any of the dates to be specified in the order, will afford evidence respecting the commission of the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004"

-- src:9135 | Form
-- src:9136 | (3) The order is to be in Form 5.0051.
@ref s 487.0141(3) (src:9135-9136)
GIVEN `the order is in Form 5.0051` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0141(3) the order is in Form 5.0051` MEANS
    IF `the order is in Form 5.0051`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The order is to be in Form 5.0051"


-- 487.0141(4) The order may specify up to 10 dates that fall within the 60-day period after the day on which it is made. "up to 10" and "within the 60-day period" are limits the text fixes: outside them the answer is JUST FALSE.
-- The 60-day period after the day on which the order is made is taken as the days from the day after it is made to the sixtieth day after (a boundary reading: fork F-EXP).
-- src:9137 | Dates specified in order
-- src:9138 | (4) The order may specify up to 10 dates that fall within the 60-day period after the day on which it is made.
@ref s 487.0141(4) (src:9137-9138)
GIVEN `the day the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the dates specified in the order` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0141(4) the order may specify the dates` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`count` `the dates specified in the order`) GREATER THAN 10 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The order may specify up to 10 dates"
        IF any (GIVEN d YIELD (d AT MOST `the day the order is made`) OR (d GREATER THAN (`the day the order is made` PLUS 60))) `the dates specified in the order` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that fall within the 60-day period after the day on which it is made"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 487.0141(5) The order may also require the person to produce to a peace officer or public officer named in the order a copy of all reports made under any of sections 7, 7.1 and 9 of the Proceeds of Crime (Money Laundering) and Terrorist Financing Act during the period the order is in effect if the justice or judge is satisfied by
-- information on oath in Form 5.004 that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the information contained in such a report will afford evidence respecting the commission of the offence referred to in subsection (2).
-- src:9139 | Suspicious transactions
-- src:9140 | (5) The order may also require the person to produce to a peace officer or public officer named in the order a copy of all reports made under any of sections 7, 7.1 and 9 of the Proceeds of Crime (Money Laundering) and Terrorist Financing Act during the period the order is in effect if the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004 that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the information contained in such a report will afford evidence respecting the commission of the offence referred to in subsection (2).
@ref s 487.0141(5) (src:9139-9140)
GIVEN `the reports are made under any of sections 7, 7.1 and 9 of the Proceeds of Crime (Money Laundering) and Terrorist Financing Act during the period the order is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004 that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the information contained in such a report will afford evidence respecting the commission of the offence referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0141(5) the order may require the person to produce a copy of the reports` MEANS
    IF `the reports are made under any of sections 7, 7.1 and 9 of the Proceeds of Crime (Money Laundering) and Terrorist Financing Act during the period the order is in effect` AND `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004 that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the information contained in such a report will afford evidence respecting the commission of the offence referred to in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004 that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the information contained in such a report will afford evidence"

-- 487.0141(6) The person must not be required to (a) produce documents more than once in any 72-hour period; (b) produce a document that is a copy of a document that was in their possession or control before the day on which the order is made; or (c) prepare and produce a document that
-- contains data that was in their possession or control before the day on which the order is made. The answer is whether the person may be required: JUST FALSE inside the protection, NOTHING outside it.
-- (a) two requirements less than 72 hours apart fall in one 72-hour period (a boundary reading: fork F-72).
-- src:9141 | Restrictions
-- src:9142 | (6) The person must not be required to
-- src:9143 | (a) produce documents more than once in any 72-hour period;
@ref s 487.0141(6)(a) (src:9141-9143)
GIVEN `the hours since the person was last required to produce documents under the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0141(6)(a) the person may be required to produce documents again` MEANS
    IF `the hours since the person was last required to produce documents under the order` LESS THAN 72
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The person must not be required to (a) produce documents more than once in any 72-hour period"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "more than once in any 72-hour period"

-- src:9141 | Restrictions
-- src:9142 | (6) The person must not be required to
-- src:9144 | (b) produce a document that is a copy of a document that was in their possession or control before the day on which the order is made; or
@ref s 487.0141(6)(b) (src:9141-9144)
GIVEN `the document is a copy of a document that was in the person's possession or control before the day on which the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0141(6)(b) the person may be required to produce a copy of a document that was in their possession or control before the day on which the order is made` MEANS
    IF `the document is a copy of a document that was in the person's possession or control before the day on which the order is made`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The person must not be required to"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "produce a document that is a copy of a document that was in their possession or control before the day on which the order is made"

-- src:9141 | Restrictions
-- src:9142 | (6) The person must not be required to
-- src:9145 | (c) prepare and produce a document that contains data that was in their possession or control before the day on which the order is made.
@ref s 487.0141(6)(c) (src:9141-9145)
GIVEN `the document contains data that was in the person's possession or control before the day on which the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0141(6)(c) the person may be required to prepare and produce a document that contains data that was in their possession or control before the day on which the order is made` MEANS
    IF `the document contains data that was in the person's possession or control before the day on which the order is made`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The person must not be required to"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "prepare and produce a document that contains data that was in their possession or control before the day on which the order is made"

-- src:9146 | Limitation
-- src:9147 | (7) A person who is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2) may not be made subject to an order.
@ref s 487.0141(7) (src:9146-9147)
GIVEN `the person is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0141(7) the order is barred against the person under investigation for the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2) may not be made subject to an order"

-- src:9148 | Expiry of order
-- src:9149 | (8) Unless the order is revoked earlier, it expires 60 days after the day on which it is made.
@ref s 487.0141(8) (src:9148-9149)
GIVEN `the day the order is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 487.0141(8) the order expires on the day` MEANS `the day the order is made` PLUS 60

@ref s 487.0141(8) (src:9148-9149)
GIVEN `the day the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day the order was revoked, if it was revoked earlier` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0141(8) the order is in effect on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the order was revoked, if it was revoked earlier`
    WHEN JUST revoked THEN
        IF `the day in question` AT LEAST revoked
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless the order is revoked earlier"
        ELSE IF `the day in question` LESS THAN `s 487.0141(8) the order expires on the day` `the day the order is made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it expires 60 days after the day on which it is made"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the day in question` LESS THAN `s 487.0141(8) the order expires on the day` `the day the order is made`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it expires 60 days after the day on which it is made"

-- src:9150 | Renewals
-- src:9151 | (9) A justice or judge may renew the order for a period of not more than 60 days on ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer indicating the reason and period for which the renewal is required.
@ref s 487.0141(9) (src:9150-9151)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer indicating the reason and period for which the renewal is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of the renewal, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0141(9) the justice or judge may renew the order for the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer indicating the reason and period for which the renewal is required`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer indicating the reason and period for which the renewal is required"
        IF (`the period of the renewal, in days` GREATER THAN 60) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of not more than 60 days"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:9152 | Conditions for renewal
-- src:9153 | (10) Before renewing the order, the justice or judge must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004 that the conditions specified in subsection (2) are met.
@ref s 487.0141(10) (src:9152-9153)
GIVEN `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004 that the conditions specified in subsection (2) are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0141(10) the justice or judge has the satisfaction required before renewing the order` MEANS
    IF `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004 that the conditions specified in subsection (2) are met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before renewing the order, the justice or judge must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004"


-- 487.0141(11) If the order is renewed, it may specify up to 10 dates during the period for which it is renewed.
-- src:9154 | Dates specified in renewed order
-- src:9155 | (11) If the order is renewed, it may specify up to 10 dates during the period for which it is renewed.
@ref s 487.0141(11) (src:9154-9155)
GIVEN `the first day of the period for which the order is renewed` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period for which the order is renewed` IS A DATE
      `the dates specified in the renewed order` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0141(11) the renewed order may specify the dates` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`count` `the dates specified in the renewed order`) GREATER THAN 10 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it may specify up to 10 dates during the period for which it is renewed"
        IF any (GIVEN d YIELD (d LESS THAN `the first day of the period for which the order is renewed`) OR (d GREATER THAN `the last day of the period for which the order is renewed`)) `the dates specified in the renewed order` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during the period for which it is renewed"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 487.015 -- Production order to trace specified communication`

-- src:9156 | Production order to trace specified communication
-- src:9157 | 487.015 (1) On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer for the purpose of identifying a device or person involved in the transmission of a communication, a justice or judge may order a person to prepare and produce a document containing transmission data that is related to that purpose and that is, when they are served with the order, in their possession or control.
@ref s 487.015(1) (src:9156-9157)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer for the purpose of identifying a device or person involved in the transmission of a communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transmission data is related to that purpose and is, when the person is served with the order, in their possession or control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.015(1) the justice or judge may order the person to prepare and produce a document containing transmission data` MEANS
    IF `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer for the purpose of identifying a device or person involved in the transmission of a communication` AND `the transmission data is related to that purpose and is, when the person is served with the order, in their possession or control`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer for the purpose of identifying a device or person involved in the transmission of a communication"

-- src:9158 | Conditions for making order
-- src:9159 | (2) Before making the order, the justice or judge must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004 that there are reasonable grounds to suspect that
-- src:9160 | (a) an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament;
-- src:9161 | (b) the identification of a device or person involved in the transmission of a communication will assist in the investigation of the offence; and
-- src:9162 | (c) transmission data that is in the possession or control of one or more persons whose identity is unknown when the application is made will enable that identification.
@ref s 487.015(2) (src:9158-9162)
GIVEN `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that the identification of a device or person involved in the transmission of a communication will assist in the investigation of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that transmission data that is in the possession or control of one or more persons whose identity is unknown when the application is made will enable that identification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.015(2) the justice or judge has the satisfaction required before making the order` MEANS
    IF `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004`
       AND `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament`
       AND `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that the identification of a device or person involved in the transmission of a communication will assist in the investigation of the offence`
       AND `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that transmission data that is in the possession or control of one or more persons whose identity is unknown when the application is made will enable that identification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004"

-- src:9163 | Form
-- src:9164 | (3) The order is to be in Form 5.006.
@ref s 487.015(3) (src:9163-9164)
GIVEN `the order is in Form 5.006` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.015(3) the order is in Form 5.006` MEANS
    IF `the order is in Form 5.006`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The order is to be in Form 5.006"


-- 487.015(4) A peace officer or public officer may serve the order on any person who was involved in the transmission of the communication and whose identity was unknown when the application was made (a) within 60 days after the day on which the order is made; or
-- (b) within one year after the day on which the order is made, in the case of an offence under section 467.11, 467.12 or 467.13, an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization, or a terrorism offence.
-- A period the text fixes: outside it the answer is JUST FALSE; where the one-year limb turns on s 2 "criminal organization" or "terrorism offence" and that answer is not given, NOTHING.
-- src:9165 | Service
-- src:9166 | (4) A peace officer or public officer may serve the order on any person who was involved in the transmission of the communication and whose identity was unknown when the application was made
-- src:9167 | (a) within 60 days after the day on which the order is made; or
-- src:9168 | (b) within one year after the day on which the order is made, in the case of an offence under section 467.11, 467.12 or 467.13, an offence committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization, or a terrorism offence.
@ref s 487.015(4)(a), (b) (src:9165-9168)
GIVEN `the day the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the day the order is served` IS A DATE
      `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `s 2 criminal organization offence: the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is a terrorism offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.015(4) the peace officer or public officer may serve the order on the person on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the day the order is served` LESS THAN `the day the order is made`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 60 days after the day on which the order is made"
        IF (`the day the order is served` AT MOST (`the day the order is made` PLUS 60)) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the day the order is served` GREATER THAN (`add years` `the day the order is made` 1)) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within one year after the day on which the order is made"
        IF `the offence section` EQUALS 467.11 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 467.12 OR `the offence section` EQUALS 467.13 THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`s 2 criminal organization offence: the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is a terrorism offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`s 2 criminal organization offence: the offence was committed for the benefit of, at the direction of or in association with a criminal organization` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is a terrorism offence` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is a criminal organization offence or a terrorism offence is for the definitions of section 2 and section 467.1
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 60 days after the day on which the order is made"
    WHERE
        `the offence section` MEANS `the offence charged`'s `section`

-- src:9169 | Limitation
-- src:9170 | (5) A person who is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2) may not be made subject to an order.
@ref s 487.015(5) (src:9169-9170)
GIVEN `the person is under investigation for the offence referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.015(5) the order is barred against the person under investigation for the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is under investigation for the offence referred to in paragraph (2)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2) may not be made subject to an order"


-- 487.015(6) A peace officer or public officer named in the order must provide a written report to the justice or judge who made the order as soon as feasible after the person from whom the communication originated is identified or after the expiry of the period
-- referred to in subsection (4), whichever occurs first. The report must state the name and address of each person on whom the order was served, and the date of service.
-- The day the duty to report starts is the earlier of the day the originator is identified and the last day of the period of subsection (4) (60 days, or one year in the longer cases); "as soon as feasible" states no number.
-- src:9171 | Report
-- src:9172 | (6) A peace officer or public officer named in the order must provide a written report to the justice or judge who made the order as soon as feasible after the person from whom the communication originated is identified or after the expiry of the period referred to in subsection (4), whichever occurs first. The report must state the name and address of each person on whom the order was served, and the date of service.
@ref s 487.015(6) (the day the duty starts) (src:9171-9172)
GIVEN `the day the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the period of subsection (4) is the one year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person from whom the communication originated is identified, if they are identified` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 487.015(6) the day from which the report is due as soon as feasible` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the person from whom the communication originated is identified, if they are identified`
    WHEN JUST identified THEN
        IF identified LESS THAN `the end of the period`
        THEN identified
        ELSE `the end of the period`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the end of the period`
    WHERE
        `the end of the period` MEANS IF `the period of subsection (4) is the one year` THEN (`add years` `the day the order is made` 1) ELSE (`the day the order is made` PLUS 60)

-- src:9171 | Report
-- src:9172 | (6) A peace officer or public officer named in the order must provide a written report to the justice or judge who made the order as soon as feasible after the person from whom the communication originated is identified or after the expiry of the period referred to in subsection (4), whichever occurs first. The report must state the name and address of each person on whom the order was served, and the date of service.
@ref s 487.015(6) (the content of the report) (src:9171-9172)
GIVEN `the report states the name and address of each person on whom the order was served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states the date of service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.015(6) the report states what is required` MEANS
    IF `the report states the name and address of each person on whom the order was served` AND `the report states the date of service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The report must state the name and address of each person on whom the order was served, and the date of service."

