§ `Section 487.018 -- Production order -- financial data`

-- 487.018(1) On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a financial institution, as defined in section 2 of the Bank Act, or a person or entity referred to in section 5 of the Proceeds of Crime (Money Laundering) and Terrorist Financing Act,
-- to prepare and produce a document setting out the following data that is in their possession or control when they receive the order: (a) the account number of a person named in the order ...; (b) the type of account; (c) the status of the account; and (d) the date on which it was opened or closed.
DECLARE `s 487.018(1) the data the document sets out` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.018(1)(a) the account number of a person named in the order or the name of a person whose account number is specified in the order, as well as, in the case of digital assets, including virtual currency, the name and account number of a person whose identifier associated with digital assets is specified in the order`
    `s 487.018(1)(b) the type of account`
    `s 487.018(1)(c) the status of the account`
    `s 487.018(1)(d) the date on which it was opened or closed`
    `s 487.018(1) other data`

-- src:9193 | Production order — financial data
-- src:9194 | 487.018 (1) On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a financial institution, as defined in section 2 of the Bank Act, or a person or entity referred to in section 5 of the Proceeds of Crime (Money Laundering) and Terrorist Financing Act, to prepare and produce a document setting out the following data that is in their possession or control when they receive the order:
-- src:9195 | (a) the account number of a person named in the order or the name of a person whose account number is specified in the order, as well as, in the case of digital assets, including virtual currency, the name and account number of a person whose identifier associated with digital assets is specified in the order;
-- src:9196 | (b) the type of account;
-- src:9197 | (c) the status of the account; and
-- src:9198 | (d) the date on which it was opened or closed.
@ref s 487.018(1)(a) to (d) (src:9193-9198)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made to a financial institution, as defined in section 2 of the Bank Act, or to a person or entity referred to in section 5 of the Proceeds of Crime (Money Laundering) and Terrorist Financing Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      data IS A `s 487.018(1) the data the document sets out`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.018(1) the justice or judge may order the document to set out the data` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer` AND `the order is made to a financial institution, as defined in section 2 of the Bank Act, or to a person or entity referred to in section 5 of the Proceeds of Crime (Money Laundering) and Terrorist Financing Act`))
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a financial institution, as defined in section 2 of the Bank Act, or a person or entity referred to in section 5 of the Proceeds of Crime (Money Laundering) and Terrorist Financing Act"
    ELSE CONSIDER data
         WHEN `s 487.018(1) other data` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to prepare and produce a document setting out the following data"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 487.018(2) For the purpose of confirming the identity of a person who is named or whose account number or identifier associated with digital assets is specified in the order, the order may also require the institution, person or entity to prepare and produce
-- a document setting out the following data that is in their possession or control: (a) the date of birth ...; (b) that person's current address; and (c) any previous addresses of that person.
DECLARE `s 487.018(2) the identifying data the document sets out` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.018(2)(a) the date of birth of a person who is named or whose account number or identifier associated with digital assets is specified in the order`
    `s 487.018(2)(b) that person’s current address`
    `s 487.018(2)(c) any previous addresses of that person`
    `s 487.018(2) other data`

-- src:9199 | Identification of person
-- src:9200 | (2) For the purpose of confirming the identity of a person who is named or whose account number or identifier associated with digital assets is specified in the order, the order may also require the institution, person or entity to prepare and produce a document setting out the following data that is in their possession or control:
-- src:9201 | (a) the date of birth of a person who is named or whose account number or identifier associated with digital assets is specified in the order;
-- src:9202 | (b) that person’s current address; and
-- src:9203 | (c) any previous addresses of that person.
@ref s 487.018(2)(a) to (c) (src:9199-9203)
GIVEN `the purpose is confirming the identity of a person who is named or whose account number or identifier associated with digital assets is specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      data IS A `s 487.018(2) the identifying data the document sets out`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.018(2) the order may also require the document to set out the identifying data` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the purpose is confirming the identity of a person who is named or whose account number or identifier associated with digital assets is specified in the order`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purpose of confirming the identity of a person who is named or whose account number or identifier associated with digital assets is specified in the order"
    ELSE CONSIDER data
         WHEN `s 487.018(2) other data` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a document setting out the following data that is in their possession or control"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:9204 | Conditions for making order
-- src:9205 | (3) Before making the order, the justice or judge must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004 that there are reasonable grounds to suspect that
-- src:9206 | (a) an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament; and
-- src:9207 | (b) the data is in the possession or control of the institution, person or entity and will assist in the investigation of the offence.
