      `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that the data is in the possession or control of the institution, person or entity and will assist in the investigation of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.018(3) the justice or judge has the satisfaction required before making the order` MEANS
    IF `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004`
       AND `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament`
       AND `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that the data is in the possession or control of the institution, person or entity and will assist in the investigation of the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.004"

-- src:9208 | Form
-- src:9209 | (4) The order is to be in Form 5.008.
@ref s 487.018(4) (src:9208-9209)
GIVEN `the order is in Form 5.008` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.018(4) the order is in Form 5.008` MEANS
    IF `the order is in Form 5.008`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The order is to be in Form 5.008"

-- src:9210 | Limitation
-- src:9211 | (5) A financial institution, person or entity that is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (3) may not be made subject to an order.
@ref s 487.018(5) (src:9210-9211)
GIVEN `the person is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.018(5) the order is barred against the person under investigation for the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A financial institution, person or entity that is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (3) may not be made subject to an order"


§ `Section 487.019 -- Conditions in preservation and production orders`

-- 487.019(1) An order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 may contain any conditions that the justice or judge considers appropriate including, in the case of an order made under section 487.014 or 487.0141, conditions to protect a privileged communication
-- between a person who is qualified to give legal advice and their client. Section numbers are decimals: 487.013 to 487.018 takes in 487.0131, 487.014, 487.0141, 487.015, 487.016 and 487.017.
-- src:9212 | Conditions in preservation and production orders
-- src:9213 | 487.019 (1) An order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 may contain any conditions that the justice or judge considers appropriate including, in the case of an order made under section 487.014 or 487.0141, conditions to protect a privileged communication between a person who is qualified to give legal advice and their client.
@ref s 487.019(1) (src:9212-9213)
GIVEN `the order` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the condition is one that the justice or judge considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.019(1) the order may contain the condition` MEANS
    IF `the order`'s `section` AT LEAST 487.013 AND `the order`'s `section` AT MOST 487.018 AND `the condition is one that the justice or judge considers appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 may contain any conditions that the justice or judge considers appropriate"

-- src:9213 | 487.019 (1) An order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 may contain any conditions that the justice or judge considers appropriate including, in the case of an order made under section 487.014 or 487.0141, conditions to protect a privileged communication between a person who is qualified to give legal advice and their client.
@ref s 487.019(1) (privileged communication) (src:9213)
GIVEN `the order` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the condition is to protect a privileged communication between a person who is qualified to give legal advice and their client` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.019(1) the order may contain the condition to protect a privileged communication` MEANS
    IF (`the order`'s `section` EQUALS 487.014 OR `the order`'s `section` EQUALS 487.0141) AND `the condition is to protect a privileged communication between a person who is qualified to give legal advice and their client`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "including, in the case of an order made under section 487.014 or 487.0141, conditions to protect a privileged communication"

-- src:9214 | Effect of order
-- src:9215 | (2) The order has effect throughout Canada.
@ref s 487.019(2) (src:9214-9215)
GIVEN `the place is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.019(2) the order has effect at the place` MEANS
    IF `the place is in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The order has effect throughout Canada"

-- src:9216 | Power to revoke or vary order
-- src:9217 | (3) On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, the justice or judge who made the order — or a judge in the judicial district where the order was made — may, on the basis of an information on oath in Form 5.0081, revoke or vary the order. The peace officer or public officer must give notice of the revocation or variation to the person who is subject to the order as soon as feasible.
