§ `Section 487.0191 -- Order prohibiting disclosure`

-- 487.0191(1) On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may make an order prohibiting a person from disclosing the existence or some or all of the contents of a preservation demand made under section 487.012 or an order
-- made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 during the period set out in the order.
-- src:9218 | Order prohibiting disclosure
-- src:9219 | 487.0191 (1) On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may make an order prohibiting a person from disclosing the existence or some or all of the contents of a preservation demand made under section 487.012 or an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 during the period set out in the order.
@ref s 487.0191(1) (src:9218-9219)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand is a preservation demand made under section 487.012 or the order is an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0191(1) the justice or judge may make an order prohibiting the person from disclosing the existence or contents of the demand or order` MEANS
    IF `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer` AND `the demand is a preservation demand made under section 487.012 or the order is an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may make an order prohibiting a person from disclosing"

