    `s 487.0191(4) another judge or justice`

-- src:9224 | Application to revoke or vary order
-- src:9225 | (4) A peace officer or a public officer or a person, financial institution or entity that is subject to an order made under subsection (1) may apply in writing to the justice or judge who made the order — or to a judge in the judicial district where the order was made — to revoke or vary the order.
@ref s 487.0191(4) (src:9224-9225)
GIVEN who IS A `s 487.0191(4) who applies to revoke or vary`
      `the application is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to whom the application is made` IS A `s 487.0191(4) to whom the application is made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0191(4) the applicant may apply to revoke or vary the order` MEANS
    IF (who EQUALS `s 487.0191(4) another person`) OR (NOT `the application is in writing`) OR (`to whom the application is made` EQUALS `s 487.0191(4) another judge or justice`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may apply in writing to the justice or judge who made the order — or to a judge in the judicial district where the order was made — to revoke or vary the order"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 487.0192 -- Particulars; form of production; non-application; probative force; Canada Evidence Act`

-- 487.0192(1) An order made under any of sections 487.014, 487.0141 and 487.016 to 487.018 must require a person, financial institution or entity to produce the document to a peace officer or public officer named in the order within the time, at the place and in the form specified in the order.
-- src:9226 | Particulars — production orders
-- src:9227 | 487.0192 (1) An order made under any of sections 487.014, 487.0141 and 487.016 to 487.018 must require a person, financial institution or entity to produce the document to a peace officer or public officer named in the order within the time, at the place and in the form specified in the order.
@ref s 487.0192(1) (src:9226-9227)
GIVEN `the order` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the order requires the person, financial institution or entity to produce the document to a peace officer or public officer named in the order within the time, at the place and in the form specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0192(1) the order contains the particulars required` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the order`'s `section` EQUALS 487.014 OR `the order`'s `section` EQUALS 487.0141 OR (`the order`'s `section` AT LEAST 487.016 AND `the order`'s `section` AT MOST 487.018)))
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order made under any of sections 487.014, 487.0141 and 487.016 to 487.018"
    ELSE IF `the order requires the person, financial institution or entity to produce the document to a peace officer or public officer named in the order within the time, at the place and in the form specified in the order`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must require a person, financial institution or entity to produce the document to a peace officer or public officer named in the order within the time, at the place and in the form specified in the order"

-- 487.0192(2) An order made under section 487.015 must require a person to produce the document to a peace officer or public officer named in the order as soon as feasible after they are served with the order at the place and in the form specified in the order.
-- src:9228 | Particulars — production order to trace specified communication
-- src:9229 | (2) An order made under section 487.015 must require a person to produce the document to a peace officer or public officer named in the order as soon as feasible after they are served with the order at the place and in the form specified in the order.
@ref s 487.0192(2) (src:9228-9229)
GIVEN `the order is made under section 487.015` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order requires the person to produce the document to a peace officer or public officer named in the order as soon as feasible after they are served with the order at the place and in the form specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0192(2) the order made under section 487.015 contains the particulars required` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the order is made under section 487.015`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order made under section 487.015"
    ELSE IF `the order requires the person to produce the document to a peace officer or public officer named in the order as soon as feasible after they are served with the order at the place and in the form specified in the order`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must require a person to produce the document to a peace officer or public officer named in the order as soon as feasible after they are served with the order"

-- 487.0192(3) For greater certainty, an order under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018 may specify that a document may be produced on or through an electro-magnetic medium.
-- src:9230 | Form of production
-- src:9231 | (3) For greater certainty, an order under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018 may specify that a document may be produced on or through an electro-magnetic medium.
@ref s 487.0192(3) (src:9230-9231)
GIVEN `the order` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0192(3) the order may specify that a document may be produced on or through an electro-magnetic medium` MEANS
    IF `the order`'s `section` AT LEAST 487.014 AND `the order`'s `section` AT MOST 487.018
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an order under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018"

-- 487.0192(4) For greater certainty, sections 489.1 and 490 do not apply to a document that is produced under an order under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018.
-- src:9232 | Non-application
-- src:9233 | (4) For greater certainty, sections 489.1 and 490 do not apply to a document that is produced under an order under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018.
@ref s 487.0192(4) (src:9232-9233)
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the document is produced under an order under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0192(4) the provision applies to the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is produced under an order under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018` AND (`the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 489.1 OR `the provision`'s `section` EQUALS 490)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sections 489.1 and 490 do not apply to a document that is produced under an order under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "sections 489.1 and 490 do not apply to a document that is produced under an order"

-- 487.0192(5) Every copy of a document produced under section 487.014 or 487.0141 is admissible in evidence in proceedings under this or any other Act of Parliament on proof by affidavit that it is a true copy and has the same probative force as the document would have if it were proved in the ordinary way.
-- src:9234 | Probative force of copies
-- src:9235 | (5) Every copy of a document produced under section 487.014 or 487.0141 is admissible in evidence in proceedings under this or any other Act of Parliament on proof by affidavit that it is a true copy and has the same probative force as the document would have if it were proved in the ordinary way.
@ref s 487.0192(5) (src:9234-9235)
GIVEN `the copy is a copy of a document produced under section 487.014 or 487.0141` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved by affidavit that it is a true copy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0192(5) the copy is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    IF `the copy is a copy of a document produced under section 487.014 or 487.0141` AND `it is proved by affidavit that it is a true copy`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is admissible in evidence in proceedings under this or any other Act of Parliament on proof by affidavit that it is a true copy"

-- 487.0192(6) A document that is prepared for the purpose of production is considered to be original for the purposes of the Canada Evidence Act.
-- src:9236 | Canada Evidence Act
-- src:9237 | (6) A document that is prepared for the purpose of production is considered to be original for the purposes of the Canada Evidence Act.
@ref s 487.0192(6) (src:9236-9237)
GIVEN `the document is prepared for the purpose of production` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0192(6) the document is considered to be original for the purposes of the Canada Evidence Act` MEANS
    IF `the document is prepared for the purpose of production`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A document that is prepared for the purpose of production is considered to be original"

§ `Section 487.01921 -- Application for review of keep account open or active order`

-- 487.01921(1) A person who is subject to an order made under section 487.0131 may apply in writing to the justice or judge who made the order, or to a judge in the judicial district where the order was made, to revoke or vary the order.
-- src:9238 | Application for review of keep account open or active order
-- src:9239 | 487.01921 (1) A person who is subject to an order made under section 487.0131 may apply in writing to the justice or judge who made the order, or to a judge in the judicial district where the order was made, to revoke or vary the order.
@ref s 487.01921(1) (src:9238-9239)
GIVEN `the person is subject to an order made under section 487.0131` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is in writing to the justice or judge who made the order, or to a judge in the judicial district where the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01921(1) the person may apply to revoke or vary the order` MEANS
    IF `the person is subject to an order made under section 487.0131` AND `the application is in writing to the justice or judge who made the order, or to a judge in the judicial district where the order was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is subject to an order made under section 487.0131 may apply in writing to the justice or judge who made the order, or to a judge in the judicial district where the order was made"

-- 487.01921(2) The person may make the application only if they give at least three days' notice of their intention to do so to a peace officer or public officer named in the order.
-- src:9240 | Notice required
-- src:9241 | (2) The person may make the application only if they give at least three days’ notice of their intention to do so to a peace officer or public officer named in the order.
@ref s 487.01921(2) (src:9240-9241)
GIVEN `the days' notice of their intention given to a peace officer or public officer named in the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01921(2) the person may make the application` MEANS
    IF `the days' notice of their intention given to a peace officer or public officer named in the order` AT LEAST 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The person may make the application only if they give at least three days’ notice of their intention to do so"

-- 487.01921(3) The person must comply with the order until a decision is made with respect to the application. An "until" bar (ruling (d) of 2026-11-05): JUST TRUE before the decision, JUST FALSE after it.
-- src:9242 | Compliance with order
-- src:9243 | (3) The person must comply with the order until a decision is made with respect to the application.
@ref s 487.01921(3) (src:9242-9243)
GIVEN `a decision has been made with respect to the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01921(3) the person must comply with the order pending the decision` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a decision has been made with respect to the application`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must comply with the order until a decision is made with respect to the application"

-- 487.01921(4) The hearing of the application must be commenced within 14 days after the application is made or as soon as practicable after that period.
-- src:9244 | Hearing
-- src:9245 | (4) The hearing of the application must be commenced within 14 days after the application is made or as soon as practicable after that period.
@ref s 487.01921(4) (src:9244-9245)
GIVEN `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the day the hearing is commenced` IS A DATE
      `the hearing is commenced as soon as practicable after that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01921(4) the hearing of the application is commenced as required` MEANS
    IF `the day the hearing is commenced` AT MOST (`the day the application is made` PLUS 14)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the hearing is commenced as soon as practicable after that period`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The hearing of the application must be commenced within 14 days after the application is made or as soon as practicable after that period"

-- the same duty as a regulative rule: the court must commence the hearing within 14 days (a clock of days after the application); no breach is stated for missing it, so none is invented: the residual obligation is printed.
DECLARE `s 487.01921(4) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.01921(4) the justice or judge`
    `s 487.01921(4) the person`

DECLARE `s 487.01921(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.01921(4) commences the hearing of the application`
    `s 487.01921(4) gives at least three days’ notice`

-- src:9244 | Hearing
-- src:9245 | (4) The hearing of the application must be commenced within 14 days after the application is made or as soon as practicable after that period.
@ref s 487.01921(4) (as a regulative rule) (src:9244-9245)
`s 487.01921(4) the hearing must be commenced` MEANS
    PARTY `s 487.01921(4) the justice or judge`
    MUST `s 487.01921(4) commences the hearing of the application`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 487.01921(4) the justice or judge` BECAUSE "the hearing of the application was not commenced within 14 days after the application was made (the text adds: or as soon as practicable after that period)"

-- 487.01921(5) The justice or judge may revoke or vary the order if they are satisfied that it is unreasonable in the circumstances to require the person to keep the account open or active.
-- src:9246 | Revocation or variation of order
-- src:9247 | (5) The justice or judge may revoke or vary the order if they are satisfied that it is unreasonable in the circumstances to require the person to keep the account open or active.
@ref s 487.01921(5) (src:9246-9247)
GIVEN `the justice or judge is satisfied that it is unreasonable in the circumstances to require the person to keep the account open or active` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.01921(5) the justice or judge may revoke or vary the order` MEANS
    IF `the justice or judge is satisfied that it is unreasonable in the circumstances to require the person to keep the account open or active`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may revoke or vary the order if they are satisfied that it is unreasonable in the circumstances to require the person to keep the account open or active"

§ `Section 487.0193 -- Application for review of production order`

-- 487.0193(1) Before they are required by an order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018 to produce a document, a person, financial institution or entity may apply in writing to the justice or judge who made the order -- or to a judge in the judicial district where the order was made -- to revoke or vary the order.
-- src:9248 | Application for review of production order
-- src:9249 | 487.0193 (1) Before they are required by an order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018 to produce a document, a person, financial institution or entity may apply in writing to the justice or judge who made the order — or to a judge in the judicial district where the order was made — to revoke or vary the order.
@ref s 487.0193(1) (src:9248-9249)
GIVEN `the order` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the application is made before they are required by the order to produce a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is in writing to the justice or judge who made the order or to a judge in the judicial district where the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0193(1) the person, financial institution or entity may apply to revoke or vary the order` MEANS
    IF `the order`'s `section` AT LEAST 487.014 AND `the order`'s `section` AT MOST 487.018 AND `the application is made before they are required by the order to produce a document` AND `the application is in writing to the justice or judge who made the order or to a judge in the judicial district where the order was made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Before they are required by an order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018 to produce a document"

-- 487.0193(2) The person, institution or entity may make the application only if they give notice of their intention to do so to a peace officer or public officer named in the order within 30 days after the day on which the order is made.
-- src:9250 | Notice required
-- src:9251 | (2) The person, institution or entity may make the application only if they give notice of their intention to do so to a peace officer or public officer named in the order within 30 days after the day on which the order is made.
@ref s 487.0193(2) (src:9250-9251)
GIVEN `the day the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the day notice of their intention is given to a peace officer or public officer named in the order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0193(2) the person, institution or entity may make the application` MEANS
    IF `the day notice of their intention is given to a peace officer or public officer named in the order` AT LEAST `the day the order is made` AND `the day notice of their intention is given to a peace officer or public officer named in the order` AT MOST (`the day the order is made` PLUS 30)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The person, institution or entity may make the application only if they give notice of their intention to do so to a peace officer or public officer named in the order within 30 days after the day on which the order is made"

-- the same limit as a regulative rule: the person may give notice within 30 days after the day on which the order is made (days after the order); no breach is stated.
DECLARE `s 487.0193(2) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.0193(2) the person, institution or entity`

DECLARE `s 487.0193(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.0193(2) gives notice of their intention to apply to a peace officer or public officer named in the order`

-- src:9250 | Notice required
-- src:9251 | (2) The person, institution or entity may make the application only if they give notice of their intention to do so to a peace officer or public officer named in the order within 30 days after the day on which the order is made.
@ref s 487.0193(2) (as a regulative rule) (src:9250-9251)
`s 487.0193(2) the notice may be given` MEANS
    PARTY `s 487.0193(2) the person, institution or entity`
    MAY `s 487.0193(2) gives notice of their intention to apply to a peace officer or public officer named in the order`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- 487.0193(3) The person, institution or entity is not required to prepare or produce the document until a final decision is made with respect to the application. An "until" bar: JUST FALSE ("not required") before the final decision, NOTHING after it.
-- src:9252 | No obligation to produce
-- src:9253 | (3) The person, institution or entity is not required to prepare or produce the document until a final decision is made with respect to the application.
@ref s 487.0193(3) (src:9252-9253)
GIVEN `an application has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a final decision has been made with respect to the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0193(3) the person, institution or entity is required to prepare or produce the document` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made` AND (NOT `a final decision has been made with respect to the application`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not required to prepare or produce the document until a final decision is made with respect to the application"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "until a final decision is made with respect to the application"

-- 487.0193(4) The justice or judge may revoke or vary the order if satisfied that (a) it is unreasonable in the circumstances to require the applicant to prepare or produce the document; or (b) production of the document would disclose information that is privileged or otherwise protected from disclosure by law.
-- src:9254 | Revocation or variation of order
-- src:9255 | (4) The justice or judge may revoke or vary the order if satisfied that
-- src:9256 | (a) it is unreasonable in the circumstances to require the applicant to prepare or produce the document; or
-- src:9257 | (b) production of the document would disclose information that is privileged or otherwise protected from disclosure by law.
@ref s 487.0193(4)(a), (b) (src:9254-9257)
GIVEN `the justice or judge is satisfied that it is unreasonable in the circumstances to require the applicant to prepare or produce the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice or judge is satisfied that production of the document would disclose information that is privileged or otherwise protected from disclosure by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0193(4) the justice or judge may revoke or vary the order` MEANS
    IF `the justice or judge is satisfied that it is unreasonable in the circumstances to require the applicant to prepare or produce the document` OR `the justice or judge is satisfied that production of the document would disclose information that is privileged or otherwise protected from disclosure by law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may revoke or vary the order if satisfied that"

§ `Section 487.0194 -- Destruction of preserved computer data and documents`

DECLARE `s 487.0194 what is to be destroyed` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.0194 the computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business`
    `s 487.0194 any document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving computer data under that section`
    `s 487.0194 something else`

-- 487.0194(1) A person to whom a preservation demand is made under section 487.012 shall destroy the computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business and any document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving computer data under that section
-- as soon as feasible after the demand expires or is revoked, unless they are subject to an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.017 with respect to the computer data.
-- src:9258 | Destruction of preserved computer data and documents — preservation demand
-- src:9259 | 487.0194 (1) A person to whom a preservation demand is made under section 487.012 shall destroy the computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business and any document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving computer data under that section as soon as feasible after the demand expires or is revoked, unless they are subject to an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.017 with respect to the computer data.
@ref s 487.0194(1) (src:9258-9259)
GIVEN what IS A `s 487.0194 what is to be destroyed`
      `the demand has expired or been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.017 with respect to the computer data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0194(1) the person to whom a preservation demand is made must destroy it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (what EQUALS `s 487.0194 something else`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall destroy the computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business and any document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving computer data under that section"
        IF (NOT `the demand has expired or been revoked`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as feasible after the demand expires or is revoked"
        IF `the person is subject to an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.017 with respect to the computer data` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless they are subject to an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.017 with respect to the computer data"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 487.0194(2) A person who is subject to a preservation order made under section 487.013 shall destroy the computer data ... as soon as feasible after the order expires or is revoked, unless they are subject to a new preservation order or to a production order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.017.
-- src:9260 | Destruction of preserved computer data and documents — preservation order
-- src:9261 | (2) A person who is subject to a preservation order made under section 487.013 shall destroy the computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business and any document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving computer data under that section as soon as feasible after the order expires or is revoked, unless they are subject to a new preservation order or to a production order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.017 with respect to the computer data.
@ref s 487.0194(2) (src:9260-9261)
GIVEN what IS A `s 487.0194 what is to be destroyed`
      `the order has expired or been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to a new preservation order or to a production order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.017 with respect to the computer data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0194(2) the person subject to a preservation order must destroy it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (what EQUALS `s 487.0194 something else`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall destroy the computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business and any document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving computer data under that section"
        IF (NOT `the order has expired or been revoked`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as feasible after the order expires or is revoked"
        IF `the person is subject to a new preservation order or to a production order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.017 with respect to the computer data` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless they are subject to a new preservation order or to a production order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.017 with respect to the computer data"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 487.0194(3) A person who is subject to a production order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.017 with respect to computer data that they preserved under a preservation demand or order made under section 487.012 or 487.013 shall destroy the computer data ...
-- as soon as feasible after the earlier of (a) the day on which the production order is revoked, and (b) the day on which a document that contains the computer data is produced under the production order.
-- src:9262 | Destruction of preserved computer data and documents — production order
-- src:9263 | (3) A person who is subject to a production order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.017 with respect to computer data that they preserved under a preservation demand or order made under section 487.012 or 487.013 shall destroy the computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business and any document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving computer data under that section as soon as feasible after the earlier of
-- src:9264 | (a) the day on which the production order is revoked, and
-- src:9265 | (b) the day on which a document that contains the computer data is produced under the production order.
@ref s 487.0194(3)(a), (b) (src:9262-9265)
GIVEN `the day the production order is revoked, if it is revoked` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day a document that contains the computer data is produced under the production order, if one is produced` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 487.0194(3) the earlier day after which the person must destroy the computer data as soon as feasible` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the production order is revoked, if it is revoked`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day a document that contains the computer data is produced under the production order, if one is produced`
    WHEN JUST revoked THEN
        CONSIDER `the day a document that contains the computer data is produced under the production order, if one is produced`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST revoked
        WHEN JUST produced THEN IF revoked LESS THAN produced THEN JUST revoked ELSE JUST produced

-- 487.0194(4) Despite subsections (1) to (3), a person who preserved computer data under a preservation demand or order made under section 487.012 or 487.013 shall destroy the computer data ... when a document that contains the computer data is obtained under a warrant.
-- src:9266 | Destruction of preserved computer data and documents — warrant
-- src:9267 | (4) Despite subsections (1) to (3), a person who preserved computer data under a preservation demand or order made under section 487.012 or 487.013 shall destroy the computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business and any document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving computer data under that section when a document that contains the computer data is obtained under a warrant.
@ref s 487.0194(4) (src:9266-9267)
GIVEN `the person preserved computer data under a preservation demand or order made under section 487.012 or 487.013` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a document that contains the computer data is obtained under a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0194(4) the person must destroy the computer data when the document is obtained under a warrant` MEANS
    IF `the person preserved computer data under a preservation demand or order made under section 487.012 or 487.013` AND `a document that contains the computer data is obtained under a warrant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who preserved computer data under a preservation demand or order made under section 487.012 or 487.013 shall destroy the computer data"

§ `Sections 487.0195 and 487.0196 -- For greater certainty; self-incrimination`

DECLARE `s 487.0195(1) what the officer asks the person to do voluntarily` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.0195(1) to voluntarily preserve data that the person is not prohibited by law from preserving`
    `s 487.0195(1) to voluntarily keep an account open or active that the person is not prohibited by law from keeping open or active`
    `s 487.0195(1) to voluntarily provide a document to the officer that the person is not prohibited by law from disclosing`
    `s 487.0195(1) something else`

-- 487.0195(1) For greater certainty, no preservation demand, preservation order, keep account open or active order or production order is necessary for a peace officer or public officer to ask a person to voluntarily preserve data that the person is not prohibited by law from preserving, ...
-- src:9268 | For greater certainty
-- src:9269 | 487.0195 (1) For greater certainty, no preservation demand, preservation order, keep account open or active order or production order is necessary for a peace officer or public officer to ask a person to voluntarily preserve data that the person is not prohibited by law from preserving, to voluntarily keep an account open or active that the person is not prohibited by law from keeping open or active or to voluntarily provide a document to the officer that the person is not prohibited by law from disclosing.
@ref s 487.0195(1) (src:9268-9269)
GIVEN what IS A `s 487.0195(1) what the officer asks the person to do voluntarily`
      `the person is not prohibited by law from doing it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0195(1) a preservation demand, preservation order, keep account open or active order or production order is necessary for the officer to ask` MEANS
    IF (what EQUALS `s 487.0195(1) something else`) OR (NOT `the person is not prohibited by law from doing it`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to voluntarily preserve data that the person is not prohibited by law from preserving, to voluntarily keep an account open or active that the person is not prohibited by law from keeping open or active or to voluntarily provide a document to the officer that the person is not prohibited by law from disclosing"
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no preservation demand, preservation order, keep account open or active order or production order is necessary"

-- 487.0195(2) A person who preserves data, keeps an account open or active or provides a document in those circumstances does not incur any criminal or civil liability for doing so.
-- src:9270 | No civil or criminal liability
-- src:9271 | (2) A person who preserves data, keeps an account open or active or provides a document in those circumstances does not incur any criminal or civil liability for doing so.
@ref s 487.0195(2) (src:9270-9271)
GIVEN `the person preserves data, keeps an account open or active or provides a document in the circumstances of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0195(2) the person incurs criminal or civil liability for doing so` MEANS
    IF `the person preserves data, keeps an account open or active or provides a document in the circumstances of subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not incur any criminal or civil liability for doing so"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in those circumstances"

-- 487.0196 No one is excused from complying with an order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018 on the ground that the document that they are required to produce may tend to incriminate them or subject them to a proceeding or penalty. However, no document that an individual
-- is required to prepare may be used or received in evidence against them in a criminal proceeding that is subsequently instituted against them, other than a prosecution for an offence under section 132, 136 or 137.
-- src:9272 | Self-incrimination
-- src:9273 | 487.0196 No one is excused from complying with an order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018 on the ground that the document that they are required to produce may tend to incriminate them or subject them to a proceeding or penalty. However, no document that an individual is required to prepare may be used or received in evidence against them in a criminal proceeding that is subsequently instituted against them, other than a prosecution for an offence under section 132, 136 or 137.
@ref s 487.0196 (excuse) (src:9272-9273)
GIVEN `the order is made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground is that the document that they are required to produce may tend to incriminate them or subject them to a proceeding or penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0196 the person is excused from complying with the order` MEANS
    IF `the order is made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018` AND `the ground is that the document that they are required to produce may tend to incriminate them or subject them to a proceeding or penalty`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No one is excused from complying with an order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018 on the ground that the document that they are required to produce may tend to incriminate them or subject them to a proceeding or penalty"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the ground that the document that they are required to produce may tend to incriminate them"

-- src:9272 | Self-incrimination
-- src:9273 | 487.0196 No one is excused from complying with an order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018 on the ground that the document that they are required to produce may tend to incriminate them or subject them to a proceeding or penalty. However, no document that an individual is required to prepare may be used or received in evidence against them in a criminal proceeding that is subsequently instituted against them, other than a prosecution for an offence under section 132, 136 or 137.
@ref s 487.0196 (use in evidence) (src:9272-9273)
GIVEN `the document is a document that an individual is required to prepare under an order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a criminal proceeding that is subsequently instituted against the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a prosecution for an offence under section 132, 136 or 137` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0196 the document the individual was required to prepare may be used or received in evidence against them` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the document is a document that an individual is required to prepare under an order made under any of sections 487.014 to 487.018` AND `the proceeding is a criminal proceeding that is subsequently instituted against the individual`)) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no document that an individual is required to prepare may be used or received in evidence against them in a criminal proceeding that is subsequently instituted against them"
        IF `the proceeding is a prosecution for an offence under section 132, 136 or 137` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than a prosecution for an offence under section 132, 136 or 137"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no document that an individual is required to prepare may be used or received in evidence against them in a criminal proceeding that is subsequently instituted against them"

§ `Sections 487.0197 to 487.0199 -- Offences`

-- 487.0197 A person who contravenes a preservation demand made under section 487.012 without lawful excuse is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to a fine of not more than $5,000.
-- src:9274 | Offence — preservation demand
-- src:9275 | 487.0197 A person who contravenes a preservation demand made under section 487.012 without lawful excuse is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to a fine of not more than $5,000.
@ref s 487.0197 (src:9274-9275)
GIVEN `the person contravenes a preservation demand made under section 487.012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0197 the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes a preservation demand made under section 487.012` AND (NOT `the person has a lawful excuse`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who contravenes a preservation demand made under section 487.012 without lawful excuse"

-- src:9274 | Offence — preservation demand
-- src:9275 | 487.0197 A person who contravenes a preservation demand made under section 487.012 without lawful excuse is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to a fine of not more than $5,000.
@ref s 487.0197 (the punishment) (src:9274-9275)
`s 487.0197 the punishment the section states` MEANS Punishment WITH
    `mode`                   IS `on summary conviction`
    `maximum imprisonment`   IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `minimum imprisonment`   IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `maximum fine`           IS `a fine of` 5000
    `minimum fine`           IS `no fine is stated`

-- src:9274 | Offence — preservation demand
-- src:9275 | 487.0197 A person who contravenes a preservation demand made under section 487.012 without lawful excuse is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to a fine of not more than $5,000.
@ref s 487.0197 (the fine) (src:9274-9275)
GIVEN `the fine, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0197 the fine is within the maximum` MEANS
    IF `the fine, in dollars` AT MOST 5000
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "liable to a fine of not more than $5,000"

-- 487.0198 A person, financial institution or entity that contravenes an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 without lawful excuse is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and liable to a fine of not more than $250,000
-- or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
-- src:9276 | Offence — preservation or production order
-- src:9277 | 487.0198 A person, financial institution or entity that contravenes an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 without lawful excuse is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and liable to a fine of not more than $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
@ref s 487.0198 (src:9276-9277)
GIVEN `the person, financial institution or entity contravenes an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person, financial institution or entity has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0198 the person, financial institution or entity is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person, financial institution or entity contravenes an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018` AND (NOT `the person, financial institution or entity has a lawful excuse`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that contravenes an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 without lawful excuse"

-- src:9276 | Offence — preservation or production order
-- src:9277 | 487.0198 A person, financial institution or entity that contravenes an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 without lawful excuse is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and liable to a fine of not more than $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
@ref s 487.0198 (the punishment) (src:9276-9277)
`s 487.0198 the punishment the section states` MEANS Punishment WITH
    `mode`                   IS `on summary conviction`
    `maximum imprisonment`   IS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`
    `minimum imprisonment`   IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `maximum fine`           IS `a fine of` 250000
    `minimum fine`           IS `no fine is stated`

-- src:9276 | Offence — preservation or production order
-- src:9277 | 487.0198 A person, financial institution or entity that contravenes an order made under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 without lawful excuse is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and liable to a fine of not more than $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
@ref s 487.0198 (the fine and the term) (src:9276-9277)
GIVEN `the fine, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the term of imprisonment` IS A `Length of time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0198 the punishment is within the maximum` MEANS
    IF    `the fine, in dollars` AT MOST 250000
      AND (   (`the term of imprisonment`'s years TIMES 12 PLUS `the term of imprisonment`'s months) LESS THAN 24
           OR ((`the term of imprisonment`'s years TIMES 12 PLUS `the term of imprisonment`'s months) EQUALS 24 AND `the term of imprisonment`'s `less a day` AND `the term of imprisonment`'s days EQUALS 0))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "liable to a fine of not more than $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day"

-- 487.0199 A person who contravenes section 487.0194 without lawful excuse is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:9278 | Offence — destruction of preserved data
-- src:9279 | 487.0199 A person who contravenes section 487.0194 without lawful excuse is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 487.0199 (src:9278-9279)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 487.0194` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0199 the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes section 487.0194` AND (NOT `the person has a lawful excuse`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who contravenes section 487.0194 without lawful excuse"

-- src:9278 | Offence — destruction of preserved data
-- src:9279 | 487.0199 A person who contravenes section 487.0194 without lawful excuse is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 487.0199 (the punishment) (src:9278-9279)
`s 487.0199 the punishment the section states` MEANS Punishment WITH
    `mode`                   IS `on summary conviction`
    `maximum imprisonment`   IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `minimum imprisonment`   IS `no imprisonment is stated`
    `maximum fine`           IS `no fine is stated`
    `minimum fine`           IS `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 487.02 -- Assistance order`

-- 487.02(1) If an authorization is given under section 184.2, 186 or 188 or a warrant is issued under this Act, the judge or justice who gives the authorization or issues the warrant may order a person to provide assistance, if the person's assistance may reasonably be considered to be required
-- to give effect to the authorization or warrant. The order has effect throughout Canada.
-- src:9280 | Assistance order
-- src:9281 | 487.02 (1) If an authorization is given under section 184.2, 186 or 188 or a warrant is issued under this Act, the judge or justice who gives the authorization or issues the warrant may order a person to provide assistance, if the person’s assistance may reasonably be considered to be required to give effect to the authorization or warrant. The order has effect throughout Canada.
@ref s 487.02(1) (src:9280-9281)
GIVEN `an authorization is given under section 184.2, 186 or 188 or a warrant is issued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is the one who gives the authorization or issues the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's assistance may reasonably be considered to be required to give effect to the authorization or warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.02(1) the judge or justice may order the person to provide assistance` MEANS
    IF `an authorization is given under section 184.2, 186 or 188 or a warrant is issued under this Act` AND `the judge or justice is the one who gives the authorization or issues the warrant` AND `the person's assistance may reasonably be considered to be required to give effect to the authorization or warrant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may order a person to provide assistance, if the person’s assistance may reasonably be considered to be required to give effect to the authorization or warrant"

-- src:9281 | 487.02 (1) If an authorization is given under section 184.2, 186 or 188 or a warrant is issued under this Act, the judge or justice who gives the authorization or issues the warrant may order a person to provide assistance, if the person’s assistance may reasonably be considered to be required to give effect to the authorization or warrant. The order has effect throughout Canada.
@ref s 487.02(1) (effect throughout Canada) (src:9281)
GIVEN `the place is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.02(1) the assistance order has effect at the place` MEANS
    IF `the place is in Canada`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The order has effect throughout Canada"

-- 487.02(2) If the authorization is given or the warrant is issued by a means of telecommunication under section 184.3 or 487.1, the order to provide assistance may be issued by a means of telecommunication and, in that case, section 184.3 or 487.1, as the case may be, applies with respect to the order.
-- src:9282 | Telecommunication
-- src:9283 | (2) If the authorization is given or the warrant is issued by a means of telecommunication under section 184.3 or 487.1, the order to provide assistance may be issued by a means of telecommunication and, in that case, section 184.3 or 487.1, as the case may be, applies with respect to the order.
@ref s 487.02(2) (src:9282-9283)
GIVEN `the authorization is given or the warrant is issued by a means of telecommunication under section 184.3 or 487.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.02(2) the order to provide assistance may be issued by a means of telecommunication` MEANS
    IF `the authorization is given or the warrant is issued by a means of telecommunication under section 184.3 or 487.1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the authorization is given or the warrant is issued by a means of telecommunication under section 184.3 or 487.1"
